# my-git's commit gate (my-rollout): <definition> TAB <test title> TAB <the case>
# -- py/my-rollout's README, "The commit gate" and "A tool adopts the commit gate".
# The tests run my-git as a program (_rt_my_git <verb>), so their text names none
# of what it calls: each verb's entry function (main's dispatch table) is linked
# to the tests that run that verb. Written once, 2026-11-23, from the tests' own
# calls; from here on the gate widens and ages them.
# 'launcher' and 'my_git_main' are linked to nothing: of the 1781 lines outside every
# function, 85 are code and the rest the interface comments above the functions,
# so a link to every test would run the whole suite for a comment. ada's
# after-check runs the full suite once per copy, and a failure this subset missed
# is bisected and linked here.
